Your 7-day trip itinerary for Madrid includes:

Day 1 (February 14, 2026): Arrival and Exploration of Malasaña Neighborhood
- Arrive in Madrid and check into your accommodation.
- Spend the afternoon exploring the winding streets of Malasaña neighborhood, known for its trendy shops and restaurants. Visit the famous Calle Gran Vía and enjoy the street performers.
- Dinner: Head to El Qu Jetcho (tapas bar) or try other local bars like The Roof, which offers a rooftop dining experience.

Day 2 (February 15, 2026): Prado National Museum
- Start your day at the iconic Prado National Museum (Museo Nacional del Prado). Consider arriving early to avoid crowds.
- Spend several hours exploring the museum's extensive collection of European art from the 12th to the 20th century.
- Lunch: Try a traditional Spanish dish like tortilla española or paella at Café Gijón, near the museum.
- Afternoon: Relax in Retiro Park and enjoy its beautiful gardens, ponds, and sculptures.

Day 3 (February 16, 2026): Royal Palace of Madrid
- Visit the grand Royal Palace of Madrid (Palacio Real), the official residence of the Spanish royal family. Take a guided tour to learn about its history.
- Lunch: Enjoy traditional Madrid cuisine at La Santera, which serves classic dishes like cocido madrileño.
- Afternoon: Explore the historic center and visit the adjacent Sabatini Gardens.

Day 4 (February 17, 2026): Reina Sofia Museum
- Visit the Reina Sofia Museum on a Sunday afternoon to see works by modern artists. Don't miss Picasso's Guernica.
- Lunch: Take a short walk to Plaza Mayor or enjoy a picnic in Retiro Park.
- Afternoon: Wander through the trendy boutiques and cafes of the Salamanca neighborhood.

Day 5 (February 18, 2026): Thyssen-Bornemisza National Museum
- Visit the Thyssen-Bornemisza National Museum to see European art from the 13th century to the present.
- Lunch: Head to Casa Mono for a Michelin-starred meal.

Day 6 (February 19, 2026): Shopping and Relaxation
- Spend the day shopping in El Corte Inglés or at other local markets like Mercado de San Miguel.
- Enjoy a leisurely lunch or dinner. Try a traditional Spanish dish like chuletón de buey (grilled beef) or enjoy some tapas.

Day 7 (February 20, 2026): Departure
- Spend the morning relaxing in your accommodation or exploring local markets before departure.
- Check out of your hotel and depart for Madrid Barajas Airport.


